From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 03:49:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Turn chunk decoration deferral off by default - it is a net
 loss

Measured on a live server, tick time per chunk went from 3.24ms to 6.81ms.
Decoration does leave the server thread - the populate path itself dropped from
2.33ms to 1.43ms per chunk - but replaying the blocks costs 4.37ms, and the
whole of that is new work.

The reason is that a deferred write is not the same write. Vanilla decorates
while the chunk is still isolated and its neighbours are not loaded, so
Chunk.relightBlock has nowhere to propagate skylight to. By the time the replay
runs, the neighbours are loaded and every write pushes skylight into them; the
profile is almost entirely Chunk.updateSkylightNeighborHeight underneath
setTypeAndData.

The earlier estimate that a quarter of population is writes and would have to
stay was measured on the cheap inline writes, and does not carry over to
deferred ones.

Left in and switchable rather than removed: the sandbox, the buffer and the
single decoration thread all work, and if the replay is ever made to write
sections in bulk and relight the chunk once, the rest is already here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/hpfxd/pandaspigot/config/PandaSpigotWorldConfig.java b/src/main/java/com/hpfxd/pandaspigot/config/PandaSpigotWorldConfig.java
index c0f61b2d1e3fc155c1ec0b224ddee256466eee19..17cbe423182b1578dab1c720a367e6d0cb09b673 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/hpfxd/pandaspigot/config/PandaSpigotWorldConfig.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/hpfxd/pandaspigot/config/PandaSpigotWorldConfig.java
@@ -94,7 +94,12 @@ public class PandaSpigotWorldConfig {
             "unchanged.\n" +
             "Decoration runs on a single thread for the whole server, so its ordering is exactly\n" +
             "as serial as it has always been.\n" +
-            "Default: true")
-    public boolean asyncChunkDecoration = true;
+            "OFF BY DEFAULT: measured on a live server this is a net loss. Decoration does leave\n" +
+            "the server thread, but replaying its blocks there costs far more than placing them\n" +
+            "inline did - by the time they are replayed the surrounding chunks are loaded, so\n" +
+            "every write propagates skylight into them. Vanilla places them while the chunk is\n" +
+            "still isolated and that propagation does not happen.\n" +
+            "Default: false")
+    public boolean asyncChunkDecoration = false;
     // Athena end
 }
